    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2003-p9.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Working outward, \\(x\\sqrt{x} = x^{\\frac{3}{2}},\\) and its cube root is \\(x^{\\frac{1}{2}}.\\)\n\nThen \\(x \\cdot x^{\\frac{1}{2}} = x^{\\frac{3}{2}},\\) whose cube root is again \\(x^{\\frac{1}{2}}.\\)\n\nRepeating once more, \\(x \\cdot x^{\\frac{1}{2}} = x^{\\frac{3}{2}},\\) whose cube root is \\(x^{\\frac{1}{2}} = \\sqrt{x}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Rewrite each radical using fractional exponents, working from the inside out",
        "The innermost \\(x\\sqrt{x} = x^{\\frac{3}{2}},\\) and each cube root divides the exponent by \\(3\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
